== Spread and influence ==

Istmo son spread from Sant Cristòfor to the rest of Balboa during the 1960s and 1970s, carried by national radio broadcasts, the BPP government's cultural programmes, and the migration of Black Balboan workers from the canal corridor to the interior cities. The genre's arrival in Sant Bart and the interior provinces produced the son de interior variant, which adapted the music to the interior community's cultural experience.

Internationally, istmo son gained its first audience in the Zong Commonwealth, where the Fosian community's cultural links to Balboa provided a natural entry point. Margarida Fàbrega's 1974 tour of the Zong Commonwealth was the genre's first international exposure, and the Istmo All-Stars toured Illypnia and Kaftia in the 1980s. The genre has a small but dedicated following in the Kaftian diaspora communities of Abyala, where it is valued for its preservation of Kaftian rhythmic traditions.

The genre's influence on Balboan popular music has been pervasive. The istmo son clave pattern and the marímbula bass line appear in virtually every subsequent Balboan popular genre, from the dance music of the 1980s to the electronic productions of the 2000s. The Sant Bart hip hop tradition, which emerged in the late 1980s, drew on the son de interior's slower tempos and its lyrical focus on the interior community's experience, and several early Sant Bart hip hop artists had previously performed in son de interior ensembles.

